                 ("p", "For most club golfers, somewhere between half and two thirds of every round. Count them honestly on your next eighteen. A bogey golfer shooting around 90 will typically take 32 to 36 putts and add fifteen or so chips, pitches and bunker shots on top. That is well over half the card, played with clubs that get a fraction of the practice time."),
